senses.gloss:
víśva [524], pron. adj.
 —1a. all, every;
every one; common in Veda, but replaced
in the Brāhmana and later by sarva, q. v.;
 —1b. víśve devā́s: all the gods, 82^1; or
the All-gods (as a class, see deva 2b),
886, 8, 90^8;
 —1c. víśvam, as n. The All,
[]
τὸ πᾶν, 92^12;
 —2. sometimes, entire, whole;
so 71^17.

√viṣṭ (véṣṭate; viṣṭitá; -véṣṭya; veṣṭáyati
). wind one's self about; caus. wind
around, envelope, wrap up, dress.
